---
// [WEB-DISCLAIMER-1 2026-09-29] /disclaimer — new legal page on the approved
// folk legal shell (layouts/LegalFolk.astro), same look as /refunds, /terms,
// /privacy, /cookies. OWNER asked for "a disclaimer page like this", pointing
// at vama.app's disclaimer (faith-based outcomes, no medical / black-magic /
// supernatural claims, acceptance of Terms + Privacy, right to change the
// service, refund summary, contact), then: "also say we dont perform any animal
// sacrifice etc, expand on such topic and add more to cover us. we do positive
// things". Adapted to Saa Thum — not copied:
//  - Saa Thum's own services only: havan, puja, satsang, sermon, meditation,
//    chadhava offerings, prasad. No astrology (removed site-wide 2026-09-27).
//  - "Only positive rituals" section: no animal sacrifice, no meat/alcohol/
//    blood offerings, no black magic / vashikaran / rituals to harm or control
//    anyone, no exorcism, no fear selling; sankalps asking for harm are
//    declined and refunded in full.
//  - Refund section SUMMARISES pages/refunds.astro and links to it. The
//    windows (24 h havan/puja, 3 days satsang/sermon/meditation) MUST match
//    refunds.astro and lib/eventTypes.ts refundWindowHours (24 / 72). Saa Thum
//    offers no rescheduling, so vama's rescheduling copy is deliberately left out.
//  - Video-only: never promise live streaming, never name YouTube.
//
// NOTE FOR AI:
//  - Shell + CSS: layouts/LegalFolk.astro + styles/legal-folk.css. Do not
//    re-derive the shell here; this page supplies content props only.
//  - Emails stay plain text "support (@) saathum.com", never mailto.
//  - No company/entity name (CLAUDE.md "THERE IS NO COMPANY").
//  - Brand text is "Saa Thum".
export const prerender = true;
import LegalFolk from '../layouts/LegalFolk.astro';
import { publicImage } from '../lib/config';

const toc = [
  { id: 'faith', label: 'Faith and tradition' },
  { id: 'positive', label: 'Only positive rituals' },
  { id: 'sankalp', label: 'Your sankalp and wishes' },
  { id: 'respect', label: 'Respect for all' },
  { id: 'no-guarantee', label: 'No guaranteed results' },
  { id: 'advice', label: 'Not a substitute for professional advice' },
  { id: 'traditions', label: 'Traditions and information' },
  { id: 'delivery', label: 'Videos, prasad and offerings' },
  { id: 'agreement', label: 'Using Saa Thum means you agree' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to our services and terms' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Limits of our responsibility' },
  { id: 'refunds', label: 'Refunds and cancellations' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact us' },
];
const lotusImg = publicImage('/assets/saathum-bright/lotus.png', { width: 320, fit: 'scale-down' });
---

<LegalFolk
  title="Disclaimer"
  titleHtml="<em>Disclaimer</em>"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lead="Saa Thum performs only positive, peaceful rituals — havans, pujas, satsangs and meditation for blessings, gratitude and wellbeing, as per Hindu tradition. The results rest with your faith. Please read what we do, what we never do, and what we can and can't promise."
  description="Saa Thum's disclaimer — only positive rituals, no animal sacrifice or black magic, outcomes are a matter of faith and not guaranteed, and how our terms, changes and refunds work."
  image="/og/terms.png"
  updated="2026-09-29"
  sticker={{ src: '/assets/saathum-booking-stickers/sankalp-thali.png', width: 1024, height: 1024, alt: 'A brass puja thali with a kalash, coconut, kumkum and a sankalp scroll — the disclaimer page.' }}
  stamp={{ src: '/assets/saathum-bright/lotus.png', width: 1254, height: 1254 }}
  toc={toc}
  railCard={{
    title: 'Faith, not a guarantee',
    html: 'Every ritual is performed in your name with full devotion. What it brings rests with your faith. <a href="/refunds">Read our refund policy</a>',
    image: { src: '/assets/saathum-how-it-works/namaste.webp', width: 550, height: 640 },
  }}
>
  <p>
    Please read this disclaimer before you book a havan, puja, satsang, sermon or meditation
    session on Saa Thum. It sits alongside our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>,
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="faith"><span class="lg-n">1.</span>Faith and tradition</h2>
  <p>
    Saa Thum makes spiritual and devotional practices possible as per Hindu tradition. Every
    havan, puja, satsang, sermon and meditation session, every chadhava offering and every prasad
    we send is provided for <strong>religious and cultural purposes only</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our priests perform each ritual with full devotion, following the traditional vidhi. What a
    ritual brings into your life is a matter of your personal faith and belief.
  </p>

  <h2 id="positive"><span class="lg-n">2.</span>Only positive rituals</h2>
  <p>
    Everything we perform is sattvic, peaceful and positive — prayers for blessings, peace,
    good health, prosperity, protection of the family, gratitude, new beginnings and the memory of
    loved ones. Our offerings are pure: ghee, havan samagri, grains, flowers, fruits, sweets,
    incense and holy water. <strong>Saa Thum never performs, arranges or promotes:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Animal sacrifice (bali) of any kind</strong>, or any ritual that hurts, kills or harms an animal.</li>
    <li>Offerings of meat, blood or alcohol, or any other tamasic offering.</li>
    <li>Black magic, tantrik "totke", vashikaran, maran, uchchatan or any ritual meant to harm, punish, control or influence another person against their will.</li>
    <li>Exorcism, "removal" of spirits, ghosts or curses, or any claim to cast or break a spell.</li>
    <li>Human sacrifice, self-harm, or any practice that puts a person's body, health or dignity at risk.</li>
    <li>Rituals that damage nature — we use natural samagri and keep the sacred fire safe and contained.</li>
    <li>Anything that is against the law in India, including laws against cruelty to animals and against black magic and inhuman practices.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="lg-note">
    <div>
      <span class="lg-tag">We only do good</span>
      <p>
        We never sell a ritual through fear. We will never tell you that something terrible will
        happen unless you book, and we never ask you to pay to "remove" a dosha, a curse or evil
        eye. Every havan and puja on Saa Thum is an act of prayer, gratitude and hope.
      </p>
    </div>
    <img src={lotusImg} alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="1254" height="1254" />
  </div>

  <h2 id="sankalp"><span class="lg-n">3.</span>Your sankalp and wishes</h2>
  <p>
    When you book a havan or puja, your sankalp — your name, gotra, family names and wish — is
    offered at the altar for the wellbeing of you and your loved ones. A sankalp is a prayer, not an
    instruction to anyone, and it can only ask for good.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may decline, or gently reword, a wish that asks for harm, revenge or loss to another person;
    to control someone's mind, love or marriage; to win something by unfair means; or for anything
    unlawful, hateful or indecent. If we decline your booking for this reason, you get a full refund.
  </p>

  <h2 id="respect"><span class="lg-n">4.</span>Respect for all</h2>
  <p>
    Saa Thum is open to every devotee, whatever their caste, gender, language, region or
    background, in India and around the world. We respect every faith and tradition, and we never
    speak against any religion or community. We ask the same respect from everyone who uses our
    services.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-guarantee"><span class="lg-n">5.</span>No guaranteed results</h2>
  <p>
    Saa Thum does not guarantee any specific result or outcome from any havan, puja, sankalp,
    offering, satsang, sermon or meditation session. The benefits we describe on our event pages
    and in our <a href="/rituals/">Puja &amp; Havan Guide</a> come from the scriptures, traditional
    beliefs and long-standing practices — and they may vary from person to person.
  </p>
  <div class="lg-note lg-note--plain">
    <div>
      <span class="lg-tag">What we never claim</span>
      <p>
        Saa Thum does <strong>not</strong> claim to cure any illness or medical condition, to
        predict the future, to remove black magic, evil eye or curses, or to produce any
        supernatural result.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="advice"><span class="lg-n">6.</span>Not a substitute for professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    A ritual is an act of faith, not a treatment or a solution to a practical problem. For any
    health, financial, legal or personal matter, please seek advice from a qualified professional
    — a doctor, a financial adviser, a lawyer or a counsellor. Please never stop or delay medical
    treatment because of a ritual. In an emergency, contact your local emergency services straight
    away.
  </p>

  <h2 id="traditions"><span class="lg-n">7.</span>Traditions and information</h2>
  <p>
    Hindu rituals are performed differently in different regions, families and lineages — the
    mantras, steps, muhurat and samagri can vary. Our priests follow the tradition they were trained
    in, and it may differ from the one your family follows.
  </p>
  <p>
    The articles in our Puja &amp; Havan Guide and the descriptions on our event pages are shared
    for general and devotional understanding. We write them with care, but they are not scholarly
    or religious rulings, and they may contain mistakes. If you spot one, please tell us.
  </p>

  <h2 id="delivery"><span class="lg-n">8.</span>Videos, prasad and offerings</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Videos</strong> — the video of your event is sent to you to download after it finishes. Start times and durations are approximate, and a technical, weather or travel problem can delay an event or its video. If we cannot perform your event at all, you get a full refund.</li>
    <li><strong>Prasad</strong> — prasad is prepared and packed with care and sent by courier. Delivery times depend on the courier and, for international orders, on customs, so we can't promise a delivery date. Prasad is food: please check the contents if you have allergies or dietary restrictions, and eat it soon after it arrives.</li>
    <li><strong>Chadhava offerings</strong> — offerings you choose are offered on your behalf at the ritual and are not returned or sent to you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="agreement"><span class="lg-n">9.</span>Using Saa Thum means you agree</h2>
  <p>
    By visiting saathum.com, signing up, booking an event or otherwise using our services, you
    confirm that you have read, understood and agree to be bound by our
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and this
    disclaimer.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you do not accept or agree with any part of them, please do not use our services. We may end
    your access to the services if you do not agree to them, or if you misuse them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes"><span class="lg-n">10.</span>Changes to our services and terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may, at our sole discretion, change or replace any part of our Terms of Service or this
    disclaimer, or change, suspend or discontinue any part of our services — including any feature,
    event, content or database — at any time. We will tell you by posting a notice on the site or by
    sending a message to the email address or phone number linked to your account.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may also set limits on certain features or restrict your access to part or all of the
    services. Please check these pages from time to time. If you keep using Saa Thum after a change
    is posted, it means you accept that change.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability"><span class="lg-n">11.</span>Limits of our responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    Any decision you make in your life, business, health or relationships is yours. To the fullest
    extent the law allows, Saa Thum and its team are not responsible for any decision you make, or
    any outcome you expect, because of a ritual, a sankalp or anything you read on our site. Where
    something goes wrong with a booking, our responsibility is limited to what our
    <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a> and applicable law provide. Nothing in this disclaimer
    limits any rights you have under consumer protection law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="refunds"><span class="lg-n">12.</span>Refunds and cancellations</h2>
  <p>
    We want every devotee to have a good experience with the havans, pujas, satsangs, sermons and
    meditation sessions they book. Because our team, priests and venues are arranged in advance,
    <strong>refunds are not automatic</strong> — they are made on request, within these notice
    periods:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Havan &amp; Puja</strong> — cancel at least 24 hours before the start for a full refund.</li>
    <li><strong>Satsang, Sermon &amp; Meditation</strong> — cancel at least 3 days before the start for a full refund.</li>
    <li>If we cancel your event, or can't perform it, you get a full refund regardless of notice.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To request a refund, send us your 12-digit UPI transaction number so we can find your payment.
    Please read our full <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a> to understand exactly when refunds are
    and aren't made.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact"><span class="lg-n">13.</span>Contact us</h2>
  <p>
    For any question about this disclaimer, a refund or a cancellation, email
    support (@) saathum.com or use our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
  </p>
</LegalFolk>
